                  "content": "Fig. 10.20: (a) Eyeglasses; (b) Smartphone camera lenses"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.578,
            0.274,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Snapshots"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.615,
            0.823,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Image formed by a concave mirror can be enlarged, diminished or of the same size as the object, and it may be erect or inverted, depending upon the distance of the object from the mirror."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.667,
            0.822,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Image formed by a convex mirror is always erect and diminished in size."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.686,
            0.423,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Two laws of reflection are:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.829,
            0.567,
            0.968,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 22,
              "bbox": [
                0.829,
                0.567,
                0.968,
                0.709
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_22.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.703,
            0.715,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "{ The angle of incidence is equal to the angle of reflection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.722,
            0.823,
            0.756
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "{ The incident ray, the normal to the mirror at the point of incidence, and the reflected ray, all lie in the same plane."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.757,
            0.823,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The laws of reflection are valid for all kinds of mirrors—plane, concave, and convex."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.792,
            0.824,
            0.826
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A concave mirror converges the light beams while a convex mirror diverges it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.826,
            0.824,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Image formed by a convex lens can be enlarged, diminished or of the same size as the object, and it may be erect or inverted, depending upon the distance of the object from the lens."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.878,
            0.817,
            0.896
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Image formed by a concave lens is always erect and diminished in size."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.897,
            0.823,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A convex lens converges the light beams while a concave lens diverges it."
            }
          ]
        },
